; Rest of the frame loop: resume, death check, tune, cheat, death, game over
;
; The second half of the pass started by #R$89AD, with five independent parts.
; All of them end by jumping back to #R$89AD (#R$8912 after a teleport or a
; death, #R$87CA after the game over), so none of them returns. Proposed split
; points are the entry labels below.
; .
; 1. $8B07 (ResumeAfterPause): entered when the pause wait of #R$89AD sees a
; key. Restores the status bar attributes (the pause cycled every colour on the
; screen) and the room's border colour, then goes on at $8B17.
; .
; 2. $8B17 (CheckDeath): if Willy was killed in this pass (#R$85D1 = $FF) jump
; to the death scene at $8C01. Then the tune: any key of the H J K L ENTER half
; row toggles it (#R$85E2). With the tune on, the idle counter #R$85E0 is cleared,
; #R$85E1 is incremented and one note is played as a short beep of 768 loop
; passes (about 9 ms, so the tune is a series of blips, one per pass): the note
; is #R$865F[(#R$85E1 AND $7E) / 2] plus 28 - 4 * lives (#R$85CC), a count of
; loop passes per half period, so the pitch drops as lives are lost. The
; border keeps the room colour during the beep.
; .
; 3. $8B70 (CheckTeleport) and $8B97 (CheckCheatKeys): the WRITETYPER cheat.
; Teleport, only with #R$85E3 = 10: key 9 held together with keys 1-5 (1, 2, 4,
; 8, 16) and 6 (32) sets the room number to that sum (0-63) and enters it at
; once (#R$8912), keeping Willy's position. Typing the sequence: in room $1C
; (First Landing) with Willy's Y index $D0, #R$85E3 counts the letters W R I T E T
; Y P E R (#R$85E5) typed one at a time; see #R$85E3.
; .
; 4. $8C01 (PlayDeath): the death scene, about 6 frames: eight rounds, each
; filling the whole room area (top 16 rows) of the screen attributes with one
; bright colour with black paper, from ink 7 (white) down to ink 0 (black), and
; a buzz whose half-period grows round by round (a falling note, from about
; 14 kHz to 2 kHz, 232 toggles in the first round and 8 in the last; the
; border turns black). Then, at $8C33
; (RestartAfterDeath), if #R$85CC is not 0 it is decremented, Willy's seven
; saved state bytes (#R$85D7, copied when the room was entered) are copied back
; to #R$85CF and the room is entered again (#R$8912) at its entry position.
; .
; 5. $8C4A (ShowGameOver): when #R$85CC is 0 the death is the game over. The top
; two thirds of the bitmap are cleared; Willy (#R$9D40) is drawn standing on a
; barrel (#R$9C60) in the middle, and a foot (#R$9C40) is drawn 49 times at
; column 15 on its way down from the top of the screen in steps of 2 pixel rows,
; landing on Willy, each time with a rising whistle (64 toggles, the
; half-period shrinks from 3,350 to 850 T states: 520 Hz up to 2 kHz)
; and a flood of the room attributes with bright white ink on a paper colour
; that runs 0-3 (the barrel stays red). #R$8574 and #R$8578 ("Game" and "Over")
; are printed on screen row 6 to the left and right of the foot's path. For about
; 80 frames the eight letters then cycle through the colours (ink (counter + n)
; mod 8, bright; at ink 0 a letter is black on black and blinks out), after which the game restarts at the title screen (#R$87CA).
; The scene lasts about 184 frames (3.7 seconds). The counter is #R$85E4.
; .
; Hardware: reads keyboard ports $BFFE (tune key), $EFFE, $F7FE (teleport),
; $FBFE, $DFFE (cheat), writes the beeper and border (port $FE), writes the
; screen bitmap and attributes.
@equ=GAME_OVER_WILLY=$488F
@equ=GAME_OVER_BARREL=$48CF
@equ=GAME_OVER_TEXT_1=$40CA
@equ=GAME_OVER_TEXT_2=$40D2
@equ=GAME_TEXT_ATTRS=$58CA
@equ=BARREL_ATTRS=$59CF
@label=ResumeAfterPause
c$8B07 LD HL,$9A00       ; status bar attributes ...
 $8B0A LD DE,$5A00       ; ... back to the screen
@isub=LD BC,THIRD_ATTRS_SIZE
 $8B0D LD BC,$0100 ;
 $8B10 LDIR ;
 $8B12 LD A,($80DE)      ; room border colour
 $8B15 OUT ($FE),A       ; restore the border
; This entry point is used by the routine at #R$89AD.
@label=CheckDeath
*$8B17 LD A,($85D1)      ; Willy killed in this pass?
@isub=CP WILLY_KILLED
 $8B1A CP $FF ;
 $8B1C JP Z,$8C01        ; yes: death scene
@isub=LD B,KEYROW_H_ENTER_HI
 $8B1F LD B,$BF          ; H J K L ENTER row (C is still $FE)
 $8B21 LD HL,$85E2       ; tune flags
 $8B24 IN A,(C) ;
@isub=AND KEYS_MASK
 $8B26 AND $1F ;
@isub=CP NO_KEYS
 $8B28 CP $1F ;
 $8B2A JR Z,$8B36        ; no key down
 $8B2C BIT 0,(HL)        ; key down: was it down last pass too?
 $8B2E JR NZ,$8B38       ; yes: do not toggle again
 $8B30 LD A,(HL) ;
 $8B31 XOR $03           ; flip bit 1 (tune off) and set bit 0
 $8B33 LD (HL),A ;
 $8B34 JR $8B38 ;
*$8B36 RES 0,(HL)        ; no key: clear the key-held flag
@label=PlayGameTune
*$8B38 BIT 1,(HL)        ; bit 1 set: tune is off
 $8B3A JR NZ,$8B70 ;
 $8B3C XOR A ;
 $8B3D LD ($85E0),A      ; idle counter cleared while the tune plays
 $8B40 LD A,($85E1) ;
 $8B43 INC A ;
 $8B44 LD ($85E1),A      ; step counter
@isub=AND TUNE_LENGTH_MASK
 $8B47 AND $7E ;
 $8B49 RRCA              ; note index 0-63
 $8B4A LD E,A ;
 $8B4B LD D,$00 ;
 $8B4D LD HL,$865F       ; game tune
 $8B50 ADD HL,DE ;
 $8B51 LD A,($85CC)      ; lives
 $8B54 RLCA ;
 $8B55 RLCA ;
@isub=SUB LIVES_FULL_PITCH
 $8B56 SUB $1C ;
 $8B58 NEG               ; A = 28 - 4 * lives
 $8B5A ADD A,(HL)        ; plus the note: D = half-period count
 $8B5B LD D,A ;
 $8B5C LD A,($80DE)      ; room border colour (bits 3 and 4 are 0)
 $8B5F LD E,D            ; E counts down to the next speaker toggle
@isub=LD BC,TUNE_BEEP_LOOPS
 $8B60 LD BC,$0003       ; B = 0: 256 passes of the inner loop, C = 3 times
@label=PlayGameTune_Loop
*$8B63 OUT ($FE),A       ; speaker/MIC state with the border
 $8B65 DEC E ;
 $8B66 JR NZ,$8B6B ;
 $8B68 LD E,D ;
@isub=XOR BEEPER_BITS
 $8B69 XOR $18           ; toggle the speaker and MIC
*$8B6B DJNZ $8B63 ;
 $8B6D DEC C ;
 $8B6E JR NZ,$8B63 ;
